## Part 1: Additional terms

### 1. Running Twilight on servers

As an additional permission, siberanka allows anyone to build, install, configure, change and run Twilight,
and changed versions of it, on any Minecraft server, proxy or network that they run or administer, including
servers and networks that earn money (for example through store sales, ranks, subscriptions, paid access,
donations or advertising). This use is a permitted purpose under Part 2.

### 2. No selling

Neither Part 2 nor the permission in section 1 allows selling Twilight. Without a separate written license
from siberanka, nobody may, under the name Twilight or under any other name:

- sell, rent, sublicense for a fee or put behind a paywall Twilight, a copy of it, a changed version, a fork
  or a renamed copy of it, or any part of its source code;
- include it in a plugin bundle, server setup, template or other package that is sold;
- offer a paid product or service whose value comes mainly from Twilight.

Copies and changed versions may be shared free of charge as Part 2 allows, together with this license and the
NOTICE file.

### 3. Credit for copied, quoted and adapted material

Anyone who copies, quotes, adapts, translates or ports any part of Twilight into another work must credit
Twilight. This covers every part, however small: a file, a class, a method, a single code block or snippet,
the implementation of an algorithm, configuration, documentation text, images and other assets. It covers
every kind of work: software, plugins, forks, articles, posts, videos, courses and answers on forums or
question sites. The credit must:

- (a) name Twilight and siberanka as the source;
- (b) link to https://github.com/siberanka/Twilight or https://gitlab.com/siberanka/twilight;
- (c) say that the material was changed, if it was;
- (d) in source code, stand in a comment next to the copied material and in the work's notices (README,
  NOTICE or credits); in other works, stand where readers of the material see it, such as the description,
  credits or footnotes;
- (e) stay with every copy and every later version of the work.

For example:

> Adapted from Twilight by siberanka (https://github.com/siberanka/Twilight), Twilight License.

The credit does not replace the notices Part 2 requires: whoever receives a copy of any part of Twilight must
also receive this license or a link to it, and the Required Notice line above. Material copied from Twilight
stays under this license in the new work; the credit does not license the rest of that work, and it must not
suggest that siberanka endorses or supports it.

Where the law allows quoting a work without permission (for example for criticism, review, teaching or
research), these terms do not limit that right, and the source must still be cited as above.

### 4. Names and logos

This license gives no right to use the Twilight name or logo except to name the source truthfully as
section 3 requires. A changed version must not be presented as an official Twilight release or as made or
endorsed by siberanka.

### 5. Conditions

Every term of Part 1 is a condition of the license. Breaking one of them is a violation of the license, and
the Violations section of Part 2 applies to it.

### 6. Other uses

Any use these terms do not allow, including selling Twilight or using it commercially beyond section 1, needs
a separate written license from siberanka. Ask through https://github.com/siberanka or
https://gitlab.com/siberanka.

